// Public synthetic BGM lifecycle example. The tone resource is CC0.

@chapter bgm_lifecycle_demo "BGM lifecycle demo"
@scene bgm_lifecycle_start "BGM lifecycle demo"

@bgm play synthetic_bgm cue=opening volume=0.04 fade=0.2

「Standalone play is fire-and-forget and starts at the authored cue marker.」

@presentation_batch policy=join
  @bgm pause fade=0.2
@end

「JOIN reaches a stable paused state and preserves the playback cursor.」

@bgm resume fade=0.2

「Resume continues that cursor; play would restart the authored cue.」

@presentation_batch policy=join
  @bgm play synthetic_bgm cue=bridge volume=0.03 fade=0.2
  @stage lifecycle_card show asset=character:sakura/smile transition=fade duration=0.2
@end

「The mixed batch uses one crossfade interval and waits for exact receipts.」

@bgm play synthetic_bgm_stems cue=opening mix=rhythm volume=0.04

「A multi-stem track still starts with the shortest play command plus one optional mix.」

@presentation_batch policy=join
  @bgm mix harmony,rhythm:0.25 fade=0.2
@end

「Stem balance changed in place without restarting or seeking the BGM player.」

@presentation_batch policy=join
  @bgm stop fade=0.2
  @stage lifecycle_card remove transition=fade duration=0.2
@end

「Stopped.」
